#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "CAP-STORAGE Object storage"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Durable object storage for tables and files, isolated per domain catalog."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: data"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Store tables and files durably, with each domain's data behind its own location and credential."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Separate locations per domain keep a grant on one domain from reaching another's files. Source files are the evidence behind every derived number, so they are kept as records ([P12]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "An object API reached by identity."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "One location and credential per domain catalog."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "An archive area for source-of-record files."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Object versioning on a lake store can conflict with table maintenance: deleted data files reappear as versions and maintenance cannot reclaim them. Use the table format's history and backups for recovery, and test the combination."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "CAP-STORAGE.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Storage exposes an object API reached by identity, with encryption at rest."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Anonymous and shared-key access are refused."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "CAP-STORAGE.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Each domain catalog has its own storage location and credential, so a grant on one domain never reaches another's files."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "A credential for one domain cannot list another domain's location."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "CAP-STORAGE.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Protection against accidental deletion is configured in a way the table format supports; it never breaks table maintenance."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Maintenance (expiry, vacuum) runs clean, and a deleted table is restored in a drill."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "CAP-STORAGE.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Source-of-record files are kept in governed storage, tagged as real, with retention set by the data owner."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "The archive location carries provenance and retention metadata."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "CAP-STORAGE.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Object storage and the catalog are backed up on a declared cadence to a geographically separate location, and a scheduled drill restores from backup outside any migration."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "The backup schedule is in code; the latest restore drill report compares content hashes and is within its schedule."
msgstr ""

